/ [ContinuationRequest] -(Delineation)> [Inside], [Outside], [References], [Uncertainty]

& [Inside] is the bounded adapter slice
  + [crate] is cantor_mcp
  + [transport] is local STDIO through the official Rust MCP SDK
  + [operator_input] is one environment file path supplied when the server starts
  + [model_input] is one strict ProtocolRequest object per tool invocation
  + [tool] is query_sop
  + [engine_call] is cantor_core execute_protocol_request
  + [output] is one existing ProtocolResponse projected into MCP structuredContent and concise text
  + [proof] is direct-core, CLI, adapter-handler, and real-STDIO equivalence

& [Outside] is work not activated by the continuation request
  + [HTTP] is streamable HTTP or any network listener
  + [effects] is file mutation, package compilation, inference calls, notifications, or external actions
  + [runtime] is resident service, session manager, or shared mutable state
  + [routing] is embeddings, learned routing, or neural training
  + [hardware] is FPGA execution
  + [configuration_mutation] is editing the user's global or project Codex configuration

& [DataDesign] is the source-projection boundary
  + [conceptual_model] is one read-only semantic request answered by admitted signed authority
  + [logical_model] is EmbeddedRuntimeEnvironment plus ProtocolRequest to ProtocolResponse
  + [physical_model] is one immutable in-process environment and STDIO JSON-RPC transport
  + [natural_identity] is request_id, environment_digest, package identity, and result_digest
  + [source_data] is operator-controlled environment file and admitted packages
  + [projection] is MCP tool metadata and CallToolResult
  + [freshness_rule] is restart the adapter after the environment file changes
  + [authority_rule] is the adapter never compiles or augments authority

& [ToolContract] is the one supported user goal
  + [name] is query_sop
  + [title] is Query governed SOP
  + [description] is use when Codex needs source-grounded Cantor terms, clauses, definitions, boundaries, relations, source spans, or proof from the pinned local environment
  + [input] is request containing an exact ProtocolRequest object
  + [output] is ProtocolResponse structured content plus a short status summary
  + [annotation] is readOnlyHint true
  + [annotation] is destructiveHint false
  + [annotation] is openWorldHint false
  + [failure] is schema, environment, trust, policy, semantic, or internal fault remains visible and never becomes fabricated SOP guidance

& [ConstraintLedger] is the non-waivable boundary
  = must: load and validate the operator-controlled environment before serving
  = must: keep tool arguments unable to replace trust roots, packages, or environment time
  = must: deserialize ProtocolRequest with unknown-field rejection inherited from cantor_core
  = must: call only cantor_core for semantic execution
  = must: preserve exact ProtocolResponse fields in structured output
  = must: advertise only one read-only tool
  = must: keep standard output exclusive to MCP transport
  = must: route diagnostics to standard error
  = must: cap environment and request input sizes
  = must: prove visible invalid-input and semantic-fault behavior
  - never: authorize through MCP metadata, descriptions, similarity, or model confidence
  - never: add adapter-local semantic ranking, fallback, or source interpretation

& [SevenFoldTrace] is the explosion and pruning record
  + [fold_1] is continuation request mapped to the previously gated CEB-014 and CEB-015 frontier
  + [fold_1_gain_delta] is explicit activation without broad activation of later slices
  + [fold_2] is MCP possibility mapped to a single user goal
  + [fold_2_gain_delta] is one query_sop tool rather than mirroring internal operations
  + [fold_3] is caller data separated from operator authority data
  + [fold_3_gain_delta] is model arguments cannot supply trust roots, packages, or time
  + [fold_4] is adapter projection separated from semantic engine
  + [fold_4_gain_delta] is ProtocolResponse remains the only semantic response form
  + [fold_5] is local integration separated from public plugin deployment
  + [fold_5_gain_delta] is STDIO only with no authentication fiction or network exposure
  + [fold_6] is success path challenged by invalid schema, mismatched environment, trust fault, and protocol skew
  + [fold_6_gain_delta] is every reached failure becomes visible tool content or transport error
  + [fold_7] is proof requirements converged on handler and real-transport equivalence
  + [fold_7_gain_delta] is adapter readiness can be established without configuring the user's Codex host
  + [pruned_material] is HTTP, UI, plugin packaging, service state, effects, adapter-local semantics, generic multi-tool API, and premature configuration writes
  + [growth_seed_set] is optional operator-approved Codex configuration, persistence benchmark, and later read-only inspect tool only after separate activation

& [AcceptanceCriteria] is the completion gate
  + [MCP-AC1] is the server initializes over STDIO and advertises exactly query_sop
  + [MCP-AC2] is query_sop advertises accurate read-only, non-destructive, closed-world annotations
  + [MCP-AC3] is a valid request produces the same ProtocolResponse as direct cantor_core execution
  + [MCP-AC4] is the equivalent CLI request and MCP tool call preserve the same semantic result, proof, and digest
  + [MCP-AC5] is malformed arguments, unknown fields, environment mismatch, and core faults remain visible
  + [MCP-AC6] is model-supplied arguments cannot replace operator-owned environment authority
  + [MCP-AC7] is format, lint, debug, release, offline, documentation, and advisory gates pass
